# Wave W17-U (Route 203): coal turf — grass greying toward coal country: a dulled green carrying stone-grey and dust-pale flecks, the sward losing its freshness as the stone thickens east (design: the grass thins, the stone thickens, the coal smoke begins). Route 203’s own ground — the greyest green in the tranche: split from Route 202’s kept petal meadow by the grey cast entire, and from Maris’s Route 111 desert turf by register (dying grass vs failing grass in sand — this road ends at a mine, not a mirage).
